{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrzMeWk6sas2G7gSwdJk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Resolution errors for indirect dependencies now name the full chain, so the vllm case reports as its-hub -> reward-hub -> vllm instead of blaming its-hub. I ran `tests/test_bootstrapper_iterative.py` and 116 tests pass.\n\nOne test fails: `TestPhasePrepareSource::test_constraint_logged_when_present`. It fails the same way with my changes stashed, so my changes didn't cause it. Its log-capture assertion sees no log output, and I didn't investigate why.\n\n**Changes in `src/fromager/bootstrapper/_bootstrapper.py`**\n- `_dependency_chain_suffix(wi)` builds `\" (dependency chain: a==1 -> b==2 -> <wi.req>)\"` from `wi.why_snapshot`.\n- `_enrich_resolution_error(item, err)` returns a new exception of the agreed type with the suffix appended. A `ResolverException` stays one, a `RuntimeError` stays one, and anything else becomes `RuntimeError(\"<TypeName>: <msg><suffix>\")`. For non-Resolve phases or an empty `why_snapshot` it returns `err` itself.\n- `_handle_phase_error()` enriches first, so test mode, multiple-versions mode and the normal-mode raise all see the enriched error. Both raise sites are now `raise err` with no `from`, still inside the caller's handler. The original is reachable through `__context__` and `__cause__` stays `None`.\n- I rebuild `ResolverException` as the base class rather than the original subclass, so a subclass such as `ResolutionImpossible` becomes a plain `ResolverException`. I did this because such subclasses may need constructor arguments. The same applies to `RuntimeError` subclasses.\n\n**Tests in `tests/test_bootstrapper_iterative.py`**\nI added a `TestEnrichResolutionError` class with nine tests:\n- the suffix format\n- each of the three exception shapes\n- the unchanged top-level and non-Resolve cases (same object returned)\n- `__context__`/`__cause__` on the normal-mode raise\n- the enriched message being recorded in test mode and multiple-versions mode"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5251,"cache_read_input_tokens":72646,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5251},"output_tokens":732,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28174ce6-2413-4fe6-a3d8-df86f8f6e70f","uuid":"c1f1a8e9-e1e9-4296-b8e3-0da7393c2bff","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:36:46.739Z","request_id":"req_011CfrzMeG6wo2dxZN4jjtt3"}
